  <content>
  <section><blockquote>The table below shows the populations of three cities during different years. Take a moment to think of at least one thing you notice and one thing you wonder.</blockquote>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
   
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        City
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        1950
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        1960
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        1970
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        1980
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        1990
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        2000
      </emphasis></entry></row> </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        Paris
      </entry>
      <entry>
        6,300,000
      </entry>
      <entry>
        7,400,000
      </entry>
      <entry>
        8,200,000
      </entry>
      <entry>
